KG42.register("edges-cb4d733f8590504af82d8d93",{"id":"S-aecaf25532e6d510","source":"KG31-623d45f464e9bce4","type":"links","target":"COMP-315d42da2c8d28d8","evidence_class":"S","scientific_acceptance":false,"relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"paper_ids":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation"],"assertions":[{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R005::E::v141-c-R005-E001","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","rule_ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R005","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"execution.energy_trade","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e15"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-623d45f464e9bce4","target":"COMP-315d42da2c8d28d8","source_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","target_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R005::V::execution.energy_trade","source_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","target_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"General P2P energy-sharing framework recorded under M01; trading within an energy sharing region. | General P2P paradigm recorded under M01; exchanges within the local market. | P2P energy sharing in grid-connected microgrids with one point of common coupling. | Simulation exit mechanism adopted in this paper; choice of trading arrangement upon termination. | Simulation exit mechanism attributed to Ref. [17]. | The aggregate retailer-trading paradigm shown in Fig. 2 for an energy sharing region.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e19"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"2e2e7fd2357976e2425787bcd53f3dd89595150feb3b2250bae322359e622eaa","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Requested quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a nonnegative net-energy bid at the relevant time step. Offered quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a negative net-energy bid at the relevant time step. The coordinator must provide and operate the trading platform and its associated metering mechanisms. Scope: Coordinator infrastructure obligations in the described local P2P framework. The coordinator does not control devices directly and applies unified rules fairly to all participants. Scope: Coordinator intervention under the paper's heuristic convergence techniques. Condition: When the heuristic techniques interfere with participants' control of their devices. Handling physical-network problems such as overvoltage and congestion is outside the coordinator's modeled remit and is deferred to further research. Scope: Limits of the coordinator's modeled remit in the studied P2P framework.","target_definition":"The energy sharing coordinator supervises the region's P2P energy-trading activities. Scope: General P2P energy-sharing framework recorded under M01; trading within an energy sharing region. The coordinator negotiates electricity purchases and sales with the retailer on behalf of the participants to balance energy within the region. Scope: The aggregate retailer-trading paradigm shown in Fig. 2 for an energy sharing region. Local P2P energy exchanges take place at the internal market price. Scope: General P2P paradigm recorded under M01; exchanges within the local market. Participants must first share energy with each other and then interact with the retailer through aggregated power. Scope: P2P energy sharing in grid-connected microgrids with one point of common coupling. Condition: The grid-connected microgrid has only one point of common coupling. P2P energy sharing is not used; all participants are instead considered to trade individually with the retailer. Scope: Simulation exit mechanism attributed to Ref. [17]. Condition: The maximum number of iterations is reached without convergence. P2P energy sharing remains in use based on the results of the last iteration. Scope: Simulation exit mechanism adopted in this paper; choice of trading arrangement upon termination. Condition: The simulation is forced to exit at the maximum number of iterations without convergence.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The energy sharing coordinator supervises the region's P2P energy-trading activities. Scope: General P2P energy-sharing framework recorded under M01; trading within an energy sharing region.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The coordinator negotiates electricity purchases and sales with the retailer on behalf of the participants to balance energy within the region. Scope: The aggregate retailer-trading paradigm shown in Fig. 2 for an energy sharing region.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":"996","section":"3.1","anchor_text":"gy sharing paradigm d P2P energy sharing paradigms. P2P energy sharing can be carried out among pros","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"P2P energy sharing can be carried out among prosumers in a microgrid or a part of distribution network (referred to as \"energy sharing region (ESR)\" in this paper), supervised by a market operator (named \"energy sharing coordinator\", short as \"coordinator\", in this paper). A coordinator is usually needed in P2P energy sharing practice due to two reasons. First of all, a coordinator is needed to specify the rules for trading and supervise the energy sharing activities. The rules include the core pricing model and implementation process, as well as other relevant rules to guarantee the interests of every participant. Secondly, a trading platform as well as the associated metering and billing mechanisms needs to be provided and operated by a coordinator, based on which P2P energy sharing is able to be conducted."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p07-c1r2__v141-a-M04-participation","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3","anchor_text":"p y/ y gy balance within the energy sharing region. P2P energy sharing in grid- m connected microgri","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the paradigm shown in Fig. 2, the coordinator negotiates with the retailer on behalf of all the prosumers to buy/sell electricity for energy balance within the energy sharing region. P2P energy sharing in grid-connected microgrids with only one point of common coupling (PCC) follows this paradigm, because the physical network structure requires that the prosumers have to share their energy with each other ﬁrst and then interact with the retailer in form of aggregated power [14–17]."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"General P2P energy-sharing framework recorded under M01; trading within an energy sharing region. | General P2P paradigm recorded under M01; exchanges within the local market. | P2P energy sharing in grid-connected microgrids with one point of common coupling. | Simulation exit mechanism adopted in this paper; choice of trading arrangement upon termination. | Simulation exit mechanism attributed to Ref. [17]. | The aggregate retailer-trading paradigm shown in Fig. 2 for an energy sharing region.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e19"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"execution.energy_trade","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e15"]},"paper_scope_note":"SDR, MMR, and BS are kept separate; the A18 net quantity differs from the A24 independent component; optional step-size control and the divergent loop in the example are not treated as general convergence or necessary dependencies."}}],"assertion_ids":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R005::E::v141-c-R005-E001"]});
